  "tines issues list": "Usage: tines issues list [options]

List issues across projects (hides done issues unless --all)

Options:
  -p, --project <name>         filter by project name or id
  -s, --state <name>           filter by state name or id
  -c, --category <cat>         filter by state category
  -w, --workflow <id-or-name>  filter by workflow
  -a, --all                    include issues in done states
  --ready                      only issues that are actionable now (not done,
                               not a duplicate, no open blockers)
  -q, --search <text>          search titles and descriptions
  -l, --label <name>           filter by label; repeat to require all of them
                               (default: [])
  --brief                      omit description bodies (saves tokens when
                               scanning)
  --limit <n>                  maximum items to return (page size under
                               --all-pages)
  --cursor <cursor>            resume from the next_cursor of a previous page
  --all-pages                  fetch every page, not just the first (slower on
                               large lists)
  -u, --url <url>              base URL of the Tines API (or set TINES_API_URL,
                               or run \`tines login\`; default
                               https://tines.tbuckley.dev)
  --api-key <key>              API key (or set TINES_API_KEY, or run \`tines
                               login\`)
  --json                       output the raw JSON response
  -h, --help                   display help for command
