",
  "tines runner": "Usage: tines runner [options] [command]

The local runner daemon

Options:
  -h, --help                  display help for command

Commands:
  daemon [options]            Run the local runner daemon in the foreground:
                              register/reconnect, poll for assigned runs,
                              execute them (\`tines runner install\` runs it as a
                              service instead)
  install [options]           Register this machine as a runner and install the
                              daemon as a launchd/systemd service that keeps
                              itself updated
  restart [options] [name]    Relaunch an installed runner service (interrupts
                              runs in flight: pause the runner and wait for 0
                              active runs first if that matters)
  uninstall [options] [name]  Stop and remove a runner's service unit (the
                              stored runner token is kept, so a later install
                              reconnects)
  workspaces [options]        List run workspaces the daemon kept for debugging
                              (--keep-workspaces)
  help [command]              display help for command
",
  "tines runner daemon": "Usage: tines runner daemon [options]

Run the local runner daemon in the foreground: register/reconnect, poll for
assigned runs, execute them (\`tines runner install\` runs it as a service
instead)

Options:
  --name <name>                  runner name, unique per user; name it
                                 machine-plus-harness, e.g. macbook-claude
                                 (default: this hostname)
  --harness <harness>            claude-code | codex | custom (default:
                                 "claude-code")
  --command <template>           custom harness command template ({prompt_file},
                                 {workspace}, {model})
  --max-concurrent <n>           maximum simultaneous runs (default: 1)
  --poll-interval <seconds>      seconds between polls (default: 15)
  --keep-workspaces <mode>       keep settled runs' workspaces for debugging:
                                 never | failed | always (default: "never")
  --keep-workspaces-for <hours>  delete kept workspaces older than this
                                 (default: 72)
  --keep-workspaces-max <n>      keep at most this many workspaces (oldest
                                 removed first) (default: 20)
  --no-cli-refresh               do not install/refresh the agent-facing tines
                                 CLI from npm (harnesses use the ambient PATH)
  --no-self-update               do not exit for the service manager to relaunch
                                 a newer daemon (only applies when launched from
                                 the daemon-managed prefix)
  -u, --url <url>                base URL of the Tines API (or set
                                 TINES_API_URL, or run \`tines login\`; default
                                 https://tines.tbuckley.dev)
  --api-key <key>                API key (or set TINES_API_KEY, or run \`tines
                                 login\`)
  --json                         output the raw JSON response
  -h, --help                     display help for command
",
  "tines runner install": "Usage: tines runner install [options]

Register this machine as a runner and install the daemon as a launchd/systemd
service that keeps itself updated

Options:
  --name <name>                  runner name, unique per user; name it
                                 machine-plus-harness, e.g. macbook-claude
                                 (default: this hostname)
  --harness <harness>            claude-code | codex | custom (default:
                                 "claude-code")
  --command <template>           custom harness command template ({prompt_file},
                                 {workspace}, {model})
  --max-concurrent <n>           maximum simultaneous runs (default: 1)
  --poll-interval <seconds>      seconds between polls (default: 15)
  --keep-workspaces <mode>       keep settled runs' workspaces for debugging:
                                 never | failed | always (default: "never")
  --keep-workspaces-for <hours>  delete kept workspaces older than this
                                 (default: 72)
  --keep-workspaces-max <n>      keep at most this many workspaces (oldest
                                 removed first) (default: 20)
  --service-manager <kind>       launchd | systemd (default: the one this OS
                                 ships)
  -u, --url <url>                base URL of the Tines API (or set
                                 TINES_API_URL, or run \`tines login\`; default
                                 https://tines.tbuckley.dev)
  --api-key <key>                API key (or set TINES_API_KEY, or run \`tines
                                 login\`)
  --json                         output the raw JSON response
  -h, --help                     display help for command
",
  "tines runner restart": "Usage: tines runner restart [options] [name]

Relaunch an installed runner service (interrupts runs in flight: pause the
runner and wait for 0 active runs first if that matters)

Options:
  --service-manager <kind>  launchd | systemd (default: the one this OS ships)
  --json                    print JSON instead of a message
  -h, --help                display help for command
",
  "tines runner uninstall": "Usage: tines runner uninstall [options] [name]

Stop and remove a runner's service unit (the stored runner token is kept, so a
later install reconnects)

Options:
  --service-manager <kind>  launchd | systemd (default: the one this OS ships)
  --json                    print JSON instead of a message
  -h, --help                display help for command
",
  "tines runner workspaces": "Usage: tines runner workspaces [options] [command]

List run workspaces the daemon kept for debugging (--keep-workspaces)

Options:
  --json           print JSON instead of a table
  -h, --help       display help for command

Commands:
  prune [options]  Delete kept workspaces (never touches a live run's workspace)
",
  "tines runner workspaces prune": "Usage: tines runner workspaces prune [options]

Delete kept workspaces (never touches a live run's workspace)

Options:
  --all                 delete every kept workspace
  --older-than <hours>  delete kept workspaces older than this
  --json                print JSON instead of a table
  -h, --help            display help for command
",
  "tines runners": "Usage: tines runners [options] [command]

Manage the runner registry

Options:
  -h, --help                     display help for command

Commands:
  list [options]                 List runners
  show [options] <name>          Show a runner
  edit [options] <name>          Edit staged awaiting-session continuation
                                 policy (runtime unavailable)
  tiers [options] <name>         Show or edit a runner's tier→model mapping
  budget [options] <name>        Set or clear a runner's money limits (per-run
                                 caps enforce now; daily limits arrive with the
                                 budgets milestone)
  pause [options] <name>         Pause a runner (stops new assignments; identity
                                 and rules stay)
  resume [options] <name>        Resume a paused runner
  remove [options] <name>        Remove a runner (refused while routing rules or
                                 pins reference it, unless --force)
  rotate-token [options] <name>  Invalidate a local runner's token and mint a
                                 fresh one (shown once)
  help [command]                 display help for command
",
  "tines runners budget": "Usage: tines runners budget [options] <name>

Set or clear a runner's money limits (per-run caps enforce now; daily limits
arrive with the budgets milestone)

Options:
  --max-run-usd <n>     hard per-run cost cap (platform-enforced on Claude
                        runners)
  --max-run-tokens <n>  hard per-run token cap (input + output)
  --daily-usd <n>       daily USD limit (stored now, enforced by the budgets
                        milestone)
  --daily-tokens <n>    daily token limit (stored now, enforced by the budgets
                        milestone)
  --clear               remove all limits
  -u, --url <url>       base URL of the Tines API (or set TINES_API_URL, or run
                        \`tines login\`; default https://tines.tbuckley.dev)
  --api-key <key>       API key (or set TINES_API_KEY, or run \`tines login\`)
  --json                output the raw JSON response
  -h, --help            display help for command
",
  "tines runners edit": "Usage: tines runners edit [options] <name>

